# DPIGate per-program whitelist (Linux)
# One program per line. Lines starting with # are comments.
# Matching is case-insensitive and a process matches when ANY of its
# identities matches — the exe path, the command line, or the kernel task
# name — so a sandboxed or just-upgraded binary is still recognised:
#   - Entries WITH a path separator (/) are matched as a
#     substring of the process exe path AND its cmdline.
#   - Entries WITHOUT a separator are matched against the exe basename
#     (exact), the task name /proc/<pid>/comm (exact), AND the full
#     cmdline (substring). Example: firefox, vesktop
# Parent processes are checked too (4 levels), which covers Electron and
# Chromium helper processes that do the actual networking.

# Browsers — basename exact match (case-insensitive)
chrome
google-chrome
google-chrome-stable
chromium
chromium-browser
firefox
firefox-esr
opera
brave
brave-browser
vivaldi
vivaldi-stable
epiphany
falkon
konqueror
waterfox
midori
iridium
ungoogled-chromium
edge
microsoft-edge

# Discord / chat — Electron apps.
# .deb install: binary is /usr/share/discord/Discord → basename "discord" works.
# Snap/Flatpak: proctrack may not read /proc/*/exe due to sandboxing.
#              → use "Bypass All Traffic" toggle in tray menu instead.
discord
discord-canary
discord-ptb
/usr/share/discord/
/opt/discord/
# Vesktop — the basename "vesktop" matches both native binaries
# (exe basename = vesktop) and Electron-packaged versions
# (cmdline contains /usr/lib/vesktop/ or similar).
vesktop
/usr/lib/vesktop/
/opt/vesktop/
/app/bin/vesktop
dev.vencord.Vesktop
# Generic Electron catch-all — gates any Electron-packaged Discord client
# whose exe basename isn't "vesktop" (e.g. unofficial/rebranded builds) on
# real hardware where proctrack has full /proc/*/exe visibility.
electron
telegram-desktop
Signal
slack

